        "title": "Smooth Manifolds",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A smooth manifold is a topological space that locally looks like R^n, with compatible smooth structure allowing calculus everywhere."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MANIFOLDS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "01-MANIFOLDS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:differential-geometry:01-manifolds, git-history:differential-geometry:01-manifolds]",
        "canonical_path": "differential-geometry/01-MANIFOLDS.md",
        "concepts": "[manifolds]",
        "current_path": "differential-geometry/01-MANIFOLDS.md",
        "id": "maxim:differential-geometry:manifolds",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "differential-geometry",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[manifolds]",
        "section": "differential-geometry",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Smooth Manifolds",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                    SMOOTH MANIFOLD CONSTRUCTION                  |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|  TOPOLOGICAL SPACE M                                             |\n|  +------------------------------------+                          |\n|  |  Hausdorff, second-countable       |                          |\n|  |  (technical conditions: separates  |                          |\n|  |   points; has countable basis)     |                          |\n|  +------------------------------------+                          |\n|          +                                                       |\n|  ATLAS  {(U_alpha, phi_alpha)}                                   |\n|  +-------------------------------------------------+             |\n|  | Open cover U_alpha of M                         |             |\n|  | Homeomorphisms phi_alpha: U_alpha -> V_alpha    |             |\n|  | where V_alpha open in R^n                       |             |\n|  |                                                 |             |\n|  | COMPATIBILITY: On overlaps U_alpha cap U_beta,  |             |\n|  | phi_beta o phi_alpha^{-1}: R^n -> R^n is C^inf  |             |\n|  +-------------------------------------------------+             |\n|          =                                                       |\n|  SMOOTH MANIFOLD: can do calculus                               |\n|  A function f: M -> R is smooth if f o phi^{-1} is C^inf in R^n |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
